kind how-do-i
title How do I activate a font file and install only that change?
intro vtium draws only the font files that batch.conf lists as active. When you activate a font file in vtium-config, the draft keeps the change until you install it. Install then writes batch.conf and leaves vtium.conf as it is, and its question says what it changes.
see fonts/try-a-font-set-whose-font-is-not-active
see fonts/use-a-font-file-that-is-not-active

# wide.bdf is installed, but batch.conf lists only mono.bdf.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
font fonts/wide.bdf 10x20
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
frit wide
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Highlight wide.
3. Press t to try live.
note vtium-config cannot try wide while its font file is not active, and offers to activate it in the draft.
4. Press y for yes.
5. Press i to install.
at the install question
check screen shows "Install the draft? 1 change to the active resources."
check screen lacks "no lines changed"
6. Press y for yes.
at the install
check batch has "fonts/wide.bdf"
check screen shows "Installed draft mine."
